1. A bearing structure comprising:  

a housing having a bearing hole extending along an axis and configured to receive a rotating shaft;  

a bearing disposed in the bearing hole and configured to rotatably support the rotating shaft;  

an oil drainage passage formed in the housing and communicating with the bearing hole to discharge oil from the bearing hole; and  

a clearance groove formed in an inner peripheral surface defining the bearing hole around the rotating shaft, the clearance groove communicating with the oil drainage passage,  

wherein the clearance groove is asymmetric with respect to a reference plane including the axis of the bearing hole, such that a circumferential extent, depth, or cross-sectional area of the clearance groove differs between opposite circumferential sides of the oil drainage passage.
